{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ImQRealityLocus","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.ImQRealityLocus","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.cal2_circle_lies_in_substrate_half_plane","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.cal2_circle_lies_in_substrate_half_plane","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ImQRealityLocus.lean#L145-L163","doc":"**Candidate (ii)'s whole admissible set sits in the half-plane, not just\n`q₀`.** The conjecture posits that CAL-2 alone leaves an Apollonius circle of\nadmissible complex `q`, with `Im q` as \"the arc coordinate parametrizing the\nother admissible q values\". Reading CAL-2 with a modulus — which is what\nproduces a circle at all — gives `|q − 1| = √k·|q|` with\n`k = Vol(4₁)/(m_μ/m_e)`, hence centre `1/(1−k)` and radius `√k/(1−k)`. The\nprobe derives **centre 1.0099145, radius 0.1000641** from the live CODATA-2022\nratio, reproducing the conjecture's own stated `≈1.010` / `≈0.100`.\n\nAny circle with centre above `9/10` and radius below `2/5` lies strictly right\nof `1/2`, with room to spare: the measured pair clears both bounds by an order\nof magnitude. So `im_qbeta_zero_iff_e1` and `im_qbeta_zero_iff_e2` apply at\n**every point of the arc**, and `Im Q_β = 0` leaves only its two real\nintersections. That is candidate (ii)'s test answered on its entire admissible\nset rather than at one point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.branches_disjoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.branches_disjoint","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ImQRealityLocus.lean#L137-L143","doc":"**The two non-real branches are disjoint**, so the extensions disagree\nabout where imaginarity is admissible *everywhere except* on the substrate.\nAt E2's locus `x = 1/2` the E1 factor is `2(1/8) + 3(1/4) + y²(0) = 1`, never\nzero — so no `q` off the real axis makes both readings real at once. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.im_e1_locus_is_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.im_e1_locus_is_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ImQRealityLocus.lean#L124-L135","doc":"**The `1/2 < x` hypothesis is load-bearing for E1** too. The branch solves\nto `y² = −x²(2x+3)/(2x−1)`, positive exactly on `−3/2 < x < 1/2`; at `x = −1/2`\nthat gives `y² = 1/4`, so `(x, y) = (−1/2, 1/2)` sits on it with `y ≠ 0`. Hence\nneither theorem above may be restated without its hypothesis.\n\nThe first draft of this witness offered `(−1, 1)`, where the factor is `−2`, not\n`0`. It is recorded because the failure mode is the point: an existence claim\nwhose witness does not satisfy the equation would have passed a reader and been\ncaught only by the kernel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.im_e2_locus_is_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.im_e2_locus_is_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ImQRealityLocus.lean#L117-L122","doc":"**The `1/2 < x` hypothesis is load-bearing for E2**: at `x = 1/2` the\nequation holds with `y = 1 ≠ 0`, so a real `Q_β` at complex `q` is admissible\noff the substrate branch. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.im_q_zero_under_either_extension","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.im_q_zero_under_either_extension","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ImQRealityLocus.lean#L105-L115","doc":"**The conclusion does not depend on which complex extension is taken.**\nStated as a disjunction on purpose: it is not that one needs *both* readings to\nconclude, it is that *whichever* one is canonical the answer is the same. That\nis what lets the result stand while `qou-c66b`'s question of which extension is\ncanonical remains open. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.im_qbeta_zero_iff_e1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.im_qbeta_zero_iff_e1","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ImQRealityLocus.lean#L95-L103","doc":"**E1: `Im Q_β = 0 ↔ Im q = 0` on the substrate branch.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.im_qbeta_zero_iff_e2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.im_qbeta_zero_iff_e2","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ImQRealityLocus.lean#L85-L93","doc":"**E2: `Im Q_β = 0 ↔ Im q = 0` on the substrate branch.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.e1_branch_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.e1_branch_pos","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ImQRealityLocus.lean#L72-L83","doc":"**E1's non-real branch is empty for `1/2 < x`.** `Im[(q+1)/(2q³)]` has\nnumerator `−y(2x³ + 3x² + 2xy² − y²)`, and that cubic-in-`x` factor regroups as\n`2x³ + 3x² + y²(2x − 1)`: a sum of three terms each positive once `x > 1/2`.\nNote this holds for **every** `y`, which is what makes the branch empty rather\nthan merely small. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.e2_branch_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.e2_branch_pos","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ImQRealityLocus.lean#L67-L70","doc":"**E2's non-real branch is empty for `1/2 < x`.** `Im[1/(q(q−1))]` has\nnumerator `−y(2x−1)` (up to the positive denominator `|q|²·|q−1|²`), and\n`2x − 1 > 0` on the substrate branch. ","signatureChunk":0}]}